  "body": "## What changed\n\nTwo gaps in the gate's unit sweep (#3173). The sweep's verdict logic is untouched.\n\n1. A link at the package level: the scan already skipped a package directory\n   that is a link, but no test covered it. New test\n   `unit_sweep_tests::a_link_at_the_package_level_is_skipped`: the scan does not\n   enter the link, the sweep removes nothing through it, and the link itself\n   stays.\n2. Case folding on a case-insensitive volume: `norm` folded case only on\n   Windows, so on the case-insensitive default volume of macOS a link target or\n   canonical path that differs only by case missed the process-check needles.\n   `norm` now folds case on macOS too. New test\n   `a_path_that_differs_only_by_case_is_one_form_on_a_case_insensitive_volume`\n   pins the fold (and pins that a case-sensitive Unix volume keeps the\n   difference).\n\n## Readings\n\n- `xtask/src/unit_sweep.rs`: `norm` (case fold), no other code change.\n- `xtask/src/unit_sweep_tests.rs`: two new tests, one borrow fix.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `cargo test -p xtask --bin xtask -- unit_sweep_tests`: 14 passed, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## What was not exercised\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` could not go green on this\n  Windows checkout, for three reasons that are all outside this diff:\n  1. The catalog tests\n     (`catalog_seed_links_face_pocket_and_drill`,\n     `committed_slot_undercut_has_its_generated_catalog_block`) read the\n     generated content under `site/content/` and `examples/catalog/`. The\n     committed content is stale against the generator in this checkout; after\n     `cargo xtask catalog` they pass.\n  2. `light_tests::the_law_names_the_light_lane_and_the_local_full_rerun`\n     greps `AGENTS.md` for LF-wrapped text. This checkout has CRLF\n     (`core.autocrlf=true`), so the match fails. A LF checkout passes.\n  3. The first gate attempts failed at build time: the gate rebuilt\n     `target/debug/xtask.exe` while that exe ran the gate (access denied), and\n     the disk ran full. Both were worked around (a copied exe, a cleaned\n     `target/`); the remaining red steps are 1 and 2 above.\n  These three tests fail the same way without this diff: the diff touches only\n  `xtask/src/unit_sweep.rs` and `xtask/src/unit_sweep_tests.rs`.\n\n## Changelog\n\nChangelog: none\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nFork synced at v0.25.0.\n\nFixes #3173\n",
